{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/46266-fae-lords-and-the-modern-world","id":46266,"title":"Fae Lords and The Modern World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T08:09:45-08:00","id":46266,"title":"Fae Lords and The Modern World","content":"How involved in the modern, mortal worlds are your Fae Lords? I don't mean Gentry politicians, but loyalist or fetch loyalist puppets running mortal power structures are all quite likely. Mortal organizations that help abduct mortals for Gentry are an interesting (and grisly) possibility.<br /> <br /> In my home champaign I am contemplating a Hellfire Club like organization of mortals with ties to a Fae Lord or two. Members are mortal magicians (ala Apostles of The Dark One from WOD; Second Sight) who serve a particularly loathsome Gentry. This group supplies mortal children for their &quot;Dark Lord&quot; in exchange for magical training, magical devices, Hob &quot;familiars&quot; and such. This club will be a serious threat, but not an overt one, preferring the shadows. The activities of fetch toughs, and well dressed Hob enforcers poking around the Hedge are just the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:02:24-08:00","id":46521,"title":"","content":"There's a True Fae in Grim Fears called the Free Market Dragon (among other things) who is really taken with free market capitalism and owns a chain of department stores. The customers tend to be very loyal, and the company's Board benefit from a number of powerful pledges if I remember right.<br /> <br /> Personally, my campaign has a Fae who has his servants placed among a telemarketing company. The calls offer to make a single wish come true, in return for a service. Heal a terminally ill child in return for killing a Changeling, that kind of thing. The group has come across plenty of humans that have been influenced by the company, but as they live in a Hollow they haven't had any exposure to the actual calls yet. It's made for a very good behind the scenes villain so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}